<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Pitt the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1759–1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Pitt the Younger was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> from 1783 to 1801 and again from 1804 to 1806, taking office at the age of 24. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-elder">William Pitt the Elder</a>, he restored the public finances after the American war, introduced income tax and led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> against revolutionary and Napoleonic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He brought about the union with Ireland in 1801 but resigned when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> blocked Catholic emancipation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-pitt-the-younger.jpg" alt="William Pitt the Younger" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Hoppner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OlderPittThe_Younger.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
